questions.text:
What is meant by the internal energy of a body (substance):
(a) the amount of heat required to raise the temperature of 1 kg of a substance by 1 degree;
(b) the amount of heat received or transferred by a body in heat exchange;
(c) the amount of heat required to raise the temperature of a substance by 1 degree;
(d) the sum of the kinetic energies and the interaction potential energies of all the molecules that make up the body.
